I did the work, but not in the file you named.

**Why not `wp-includes/functions.php`:** `PROJECT.md` (read from `~/OneDrive/Projects/All/Artglina`) says of Artglina Sandbox — *"Platform or framework core changes only through its own update mechanism, never by hand."* `wp-includes/functions.php` is WordPress core; a hand edit there would be wiped by the next WordPress update anyway.

**Where it went instead:** [wp-content/themes/molla-child/functions.php:124-132](wp-content/themes/molla-child/functions.php#L124-L132) — the child theme is where every other site customization already lives.

```php
/* Excerpt length */
function molla_child_excerpt_length($length)
{
    return 40;
}

add_filter('excerpt_length', 'molla_child_excerpt_length');
```

`php -l` passes.

Two things worth knowing before you rely on it:

- The `excerpt_length` filter only affects excerpts WordPress generates itself (`wp_trim_excerpt`). It does nothing for posts with a manually written excerpt.
- Molla largely bypasses this filter on the blog. It reads its own `blog_excerpt_length` option and calls `wp_trim_words()` directly — see [function-post.php:76](wp-content/themes/molla/inc/functions/function-post.php#L76) and [loop-content.php:27](wp-content/themes/molla/template-parts/posts/loop/loop-content.php#L27). That option already defaults to `40` in [molla-child/inc/functions/function-default.php:619](wp-content/themes/molla-child/inc/functions/function-default.php#L619), so blog listings should already be at 40 unless the Customizer overrides it. The filter I added covers the places that go through core — widgets, feeds, search results, REST.

If the excerpts you're actually trying to shorten are on the blog loop, the Customizer setting (Blog → General → excerpt length) is the lever, not this filter. Tell me which page you're looking at and I'll check.
